WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.251
- (sighs) I don't know if I can do this.

00:00:02.251 --> 00:00:06.580
(groaning) I'd really
like to go back in time,

00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:10.280
and punch myself for thinking
this was a good idea.

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:12.863
(upbeat music)

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:17.520
Every year, there is a
worldwide challenge called,

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:19.070
National Novel Writing Month.

00:00:19.070 --> 00:00:20.650
Also known as, NaNoWriMo.

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:22.010
And this takes place every year

00:00:22.010 --> 00:00:23.070
during the month of November.

00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:24.460
And the challenge is to write

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:27.070
50,000 words in those 30 days.

00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:29.360
It's absolutely ridiculous,
and absurd, and crazy.

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:31.410
So, of course, I'm gonna do it.

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:32.660
But I'm taking on this challenge

00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:36.820
because I am a type of person
who never finishes anything.

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:39.770
So, maybe if I vlog the
entire thing and I do this,

00:00:39.770 --> 00:00:42.770
I can actually finish a book in 30 days.

00:00:42.770 --> 00:00:44.270
It is two days away from November.

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:45.410
But I've already written an outline,

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:47.970
I have a pretty good idea of
the story I'm going to write.

00:00:47.970 --> 00:00:49.670
And hopefully I can do this.

00:00:49.670 --> 00:00:50.503
Wish me luck!

00:00:50.503 --> 00:00:55.210
So, theoretically, I should
write 1,667 words a day

00:00:55.210 --> 00:00:57.110
to get to 50,000 by the end of the month.

00:00:57.110 --> 00:00:59.660
But realistically, that's
probably not gonna happen.

00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:02.710
So, today, my goal is 3,000 words.

00:01:02.710 --> 00:01:03.760
I'm trying to start off strong,

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:04.890
because I know later in the month,

00:01:04.890 --> 00:01:06.760
I'm not going to do as well.

00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:09.093
(fun music)

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:14.420
Okay, it's been about an hour and a half

00:01:15.483 --> 00:01:19.290
and I have written 2,289 words.

00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:20.123
What's up?

00:01:20.123 --> 00:01:22.420
I'm going to an official
NoNoWriMo event later today,

00:01:22.420 --> 00:01:23.940
and I'm gonna write so much more.

00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:25.350
I broke 5,000 words today,

00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:27.550
which is way more than I was planning,

00:01:27.550 --> 00:01:29.260
and way more than I anticipated.

00:01:29.260 --> 00:01:32.290
I got my coffee, I'm ready to
rock, ready to be energized.

00:01:32.290 --> 00:01:33.420
I am officially done for the day

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:38.420
because I just wrote
3,223 words (chuckles).

00:01:38.710 --> 00:01:43.680
Which brings me to a total of 8,291 words

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:46.000
on day two (chuckles).

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:47.300
I am on fire.

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:50.010
So, it's somehow day six.

00:01:50.010 --> 00:01:52.070
I'm not sure how I got here (chuckles).

00:01:52.070 --> 00:01:53.990
I wrote a little over 2,000 words today.

00:01:53.990 --> 00:01:56.440
And it was kind of a
struggle to get there.

00:01:56.440 --> 00:01:59.950
This is the first time I
have just kind of hit a wall.

00:01:59.950 --> 00:02:02.710
I wrote over 4,000 words today,
which is pretty damn good.

00:02:02.710 --> 00:02:04.340
I have been significantly

00:02:04.340 --> 00:02:07.310
slowing down in my writing process.

00:02:07.310 --> 00:02:08.990
I don't know why, it's
just been really hard

00:02:08.990 --> 00:02:11.761
to hit even like 1,000 words.

00:02:11.761 --> 00:02:14.010
(sighs) I don't know if I can do this.

00:02:14.010 --> 00:02:18.300
After a very long time of just
excruciating writer's block,

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:22.440
I have finally reached 25,000 words!

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:25.440
I'm halfway there,
guys, I'm halfway there!

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:27.190
I realized today that I haven't really

00:02:27.190 --> 00:02:29.190
told you what my book's about.

00:02:29.190 --> 00:02:32.200
So, basically, I am writing
a young adult fantasy novel.

00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:34.010
And the story follows two twins.

00:02:34.010 --> 00:02:37.760
And they discover this circular
room full of seven doors.

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:41.380
And they learn that each door
leads to a different world.

00:02:41.380 --> 00:02:43.570
It would be like if one
door lead to Narnia,

00:02:43.570 --> 00:02:45.300
one door lead to Hogwarts.

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:47.060
So, the twins go through these doors,

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:48.520
and they go on this crazy adventure.

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:50.660
And I'm not going to tell
you anything more than that.

00:02:50.660 --> 00:02:52.370
But I feel like at the end of this month,

00:02:52.370 --> 00:02:54.030
I'll at least have some bare bones

00:02:54.030 --> 00:02:55.320
of something to work with.

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:57.630
'Cause before any of this,
all it was was an idea.

00:02:57.630 --> 00:02:58.825
At least I hope so.

00:02:58.825 --> 00:03:01.075
(groaning)

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:09.500
I haven't written in five days.

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:10.960
Why do I keep doing this?

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:12.440
Why does this keep happening?

00:03:12.440 --> 00:03:14.610
All right, this is it,
this is the last straw.

00:03:14.610 --> 00:03:17.080
It is November 20th, I'm
gonna write every day.

00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:18.881
I'm gonna do this, I'm gonna do this.

00:03:18.881 --> 00:03:20.482
I am going to do this.

00:03:20.482 --> 00:03:22.574
(upbeat music)

00:03:22.574 --> 00:03:25.530
Okay, so this is becoming
a recurring thing for me.

00:03:25.530 --> 00:03:27.880
Thanksgiving break was a thing,

00:03:27.880 --> 00:03:29.660
and I went home to see my family.

00:03:29.660 --> 00:03:33.380
I had a great time, but I
didn't write a single word.

00:03:33.380 --> 00:03:37.380
So, I haven't written in about six days.

00:03:38.330 --> 00:03:40.750
It's November 27th, I have literally

00:03:40.750 --> 00:03:43.170
four days to finish this book.

00:03:43.170 --> 00:03:45.290
This whole time, I was
like, "This is hard.

00:03:45.290 --> 00:03:46.850
"I'm struggling, but I can do it.

00:03:46.850 --> 00:03:47.960
"I'm gonna do this."

00:03:47.960 --> 00:03:49.070
And now, I'm getting to the point,

00:03:49.070 --> 00:03:52.750
where I don't know if I can do this.

00:03:52.750 --> 00:03:55.520
Okay, we're at the very
last NaNoWriMo event.

00:03:55.520 --> 00:03:59.080
We are pretty much the
last people here (laughs).

00:04:00.350 --> 00:04:04.320
And look at this, look at
this, look at this (yells).

00:04:05.912 --> 00:04:06.900
It's the home stretch now.

00:04:06.900 --> 00:04:09.000
It's the home stretch,
we can do this, let's go.

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:11.860
I'm gonna do it for the
first time this month,

00:04:11.860 --> 00:04:14.730
I am officially confident enough to say

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:17.400
that I am going to finish NaNoWriMo.

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:20.000
I am going to write
50,000 words in 30 days.

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:21.720
And it feels so good to say that.

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:26.320
I just hit 45,000 words, and
tomorrow is the last day.

00:04:26.320 --> 00:04:29.480
Which means I have to
write 5,000 words tomorrow.

00:04:29.480 --> 00:04:31.000
And that's it (sighs), my God.

00:04:32.390 --> 00:04:34.330
This is such an incredible feeling.

00:04:34.330 --> 00:04:36.160
I can't even explain it to it.

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:36.993
It's just--

00:04:38.820 --> 00:04:40.030
I'm so proud.

00:04:40.030 --> 00:04:43.720
Today is the last day
of NaNoWriMo (chuckles).

00:04:43.720 --> 00:04:46.040
I have a little bit less
than 5,000 words left.

00:04:46.040 --> 00:04:48.530
I think I can do it, that
seems pretty reasonable.

00:04:48.530 --> 00:04:50.940
In one day, and once today is over,

00:04:50.940 --> 00:04:53.734
I will have written 50,000
words, and I will be done.

00:04:53.734 --> 00:04:55.300
(sighs) Oh, my God.

00:04:55.300 --> 00:04:56.930
38 words left (chuckles).

00:04:58.982 --> 00:05:01.649
(intense music)

00:05:12.134 --> 00:05:15.940
50,000 words, 50,000 words, 50,000 words.

00:05:15.940 --> 00:05:18.724
Technically, 50,011 words.

00:05:18.724 --> 00:05:22.193
Oh, my God.

00:05:22.193 --> 00:05:27.193
(sighs) I honestly cannot
believe that this is over.

00:05:27.250 --> 00:05:29.220
What an incredible experience, honestly.

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:32.420
Like, challenging myself
to do this was so hard.

00:05:32.420 --> 00:05:35.490
But really fun for the parts
that it wasn't killing me,

00:05:35.490 --> 00:05:36.440
it was really fun (chuckles).

00:05:36.440 --> 00:05:38.850
And to celebrate, I'm gonna
go print out my entire book,

00:05:38.850 --> 00:05:40.300
so that I can hold it in my hands,

00:05:40.300 --> 00:05:43.094
and just physically see my accomplishment.

00:05:43.094 --> 00:05:46.380
(printer whirring)

00:05:46.380 --> 00:05:47.213
I have it.

00:05:47.213 --> 00:05:48.930
This is still pretty awesome
to be able to hold this

00:05:48.930 --> 00:05:51.684
in my hand and say I wrote all of it.

00:05:51.684 --> 00:05:53.267
- You wrote a book?

00:05:55.382 --> 00:05:56.810
Aw, what the heck?

00:05:56.810 --> 00:05:58.433
- [Steph] I wrote it in 30 days.

00:05:58.433 --> 00:06:00.690
(gasps)
- Oh, my God.

00:06:00.690 --> 00:06:04.770
Actually holding this,
this is so many pages.

00:06:04.770 --> 00:06:07.694
That is insane, actually,
now that I think about it.

00:06:07.694 --> 00:06:09.210
- Wait, what the what?

00:06:09.210 --> 00:06:10.043
What the heck?

00:06:10.043 --> 00:06:11.630
How did you do this?

00:06:11.630 --> 00:06:13.010
Where did you do this?

00:06:13.010 --> 00:06:13.960
I don't get it.

00:06:13.960 --> 00:06:16.360
- Moving forward, I
think I'm going to read

00:06:16.360 --> 00:06:20.350
my entire thing, edit it, fix
all the very sloppy mistakes

00:06:20.350 --> 00:06:21.740
that I'm sure I made while I was trying

00:06:21.740 --> 00:06:24.410
to just push through these 30 days.

00:06:24.410 --> 00:06:27.740
And then, I'm gonna find an
editor, maybe find an agent.

00:06:27.740 --> 00:06:30.060
Not sure how to do that
(chuckles), but it's gonna happen.

00:06:30.060 --> 00:06:31.920
And maybe, hopefully, one day,

00:06:31.920 --> 00:06:34.700
my book with be in your local bookstore.

00:06:34.700 --> 00:06:36.500
But honestly, this was
such a great experience.

00:06:36.500 --> 00:06:38.070
I'm so excited for everyone else

00:06:38.070 --> 00:06:39.380
who participated in NaNoWriMo,

00:06:39.380 --> 00:06:40.860
and everyone else who completed it,

00:06:40.860 --> 00:06:42.140
and finished their goal.

00:06:42.140 --> 00:06:44.180
Like, that's so hard, good for you.

00:06:44.180 --> 00:06:45.160
High five, team.

00:06:45.160 --> 00:06:47.913
Maybe I'll see you again
next year, NaNoWriMo.

00:06:47.913 --> 00:06:50.996
(lighthearted music)

